{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And he bought the parcel of the field.</b> Because he wanted to build an altar there, therefore he did not wish to bring offerings to HaShem for free, as David did at the threshing floor of Araunah the Jebusite (II Samuel 24:24). And Scripture told us that he bought it for a hundred kesitah, corresponding to the altar in the eternal Temple, which was a hundred cubits high, to atone for every sin that stems from the sin of the first man, who was created from one end of the heavens to the other, and was diminished by his sin and stood at a hundred cubits. Therefore the Temple was a hundred cubits high, for from there man was formed — from the place concerning which it is stated (Exodus 20:21), ״מִזְבַּח אֲדָמָה תַּעֲשֶׂה לִּי״, for the place of the earth was also a cause of the sin, as explained above in parashat Bereishit on the verse ״וַתּוֹצֵא הָאָרֶץ וְגוֹ׳ עֵץ פְּרִי״ (Genesis 1:12). Therefore Scripture told us that he acquired this place for an altar for a hundred kesitah." "And what he wrote: ״וַיִּקְרָא לוֹ אֵל אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״. And our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Megillah 18) that the Holy One, blessed be He, called Jacob ״אֵל״. The reason for this: for Jacob said, ״וְכֹל אֲשֶׁר תִּתֶּן לִי עַשֵּׂר אֲעַשְּׂרֶנּוּ לָךְ״ (Genesis 28:22); therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, gave him also the tithe from the three hundred and ten hidden worlds belonging to every righteous person in the world to come, and gave him from them in this world the tithe, which amounts to the number thirty-one; therefore He called him ״אֵל״. And further: daughters take a tithe of property, and in this world we are likened to females, for all is suffering; but in the world to come they will be like males who do not give birth, and then He will bequeath them all three hundred and ten worlds. And for this reason this world is with the letter heh, corresponding to the heh in ״אִשָּׁה״, and the world to come is with the letter yod, corresponding to the yod in ״אִישׁ״, and it is easy to understand."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:31:59.819242114Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}